## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical use of PIM, approvals, MFA, and auditing in real admin flows.

## Key Concepts

- Privileged Identity Management
- Just-In-Time access
- MFA and approvals
- Activation duration and auto-revoke
- Auditing and alerts

## Code Example

```javascript
// PIM-like REST flow (illustrative)
async function activatePIM() {
  const token = await getGraphToken(['PrivilegedIdentityManagement.Read.All']);
  const res = await fetch('https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/privilegedRoleAssignments', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      roleDefinitionId: '<role-id>',
      scope: '<scope>',
      duration: 'PT1H',
      activationApprover: '<manager@contoso.com>'
    })
  });
  return res.json();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle emergency access without cascading approvals?
- What CA or BA policies would guard this flow during off-hours?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes real-world governance for privileged access, focusing on JIT, approvals, and audit trail at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Privileged Identity Management (PIM)
- Just-In-Time (JIT) elevation
- Approval workflows and MFA enforcement
- Activation windows, justification, auto-revocation
- Audit trails, post-activation reviews, sandbox testing

## Code Example
```javascript
async function requestPimActivation(userId, roleId, durationHrs, justification){
  const token = await getAadToken();
  const res = await fetch(`https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/privilegedRoles/${roleId}/activate`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type':'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ principalId: userId, duration: `PT${durationHrs}H`, reason: justification, notifyUsers: true })
  });
  return res.json();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the audit trail against compliance requirements?
- What failure modes require immediate auto-revocation and how would you test them?
